    ("A person walks 3 km West, turns left and walks 4 km. How far is he from his starting point?", "5 km. Forms a right-angled triangle with sides 3 km and 4 km. By Pythagoras theorem: Distance = sqrt(3^2 + 4^2) = sqrt(9 + 16) = sqrt(25) = 5 km South-West.", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What is the direction from start?"),
    ("One morning after sunrise, Suresh was standing facing a pole. The shadow of the pole fell exactly to his right. In which direction was Suresh facing?", "South. In the morning, the Sun is in the East, so shadows fall towards the West. If the shadow is to Suresh's right, West is to his right. Facing South puts West on the right.", "Intermediate", "Problem Solving", "", "What if it was evening sunset?"),
    ("A's mother is B's sister and has a daughter C. How can A be related to B?", "Nephew or Niece. B is the maternal uncle or aunt. A is B's sister's child.", "Easy", "Concept", "", "What if A is female?"),
