    ("Direction Sense MCQ: A man travels 12 km North, then 5 km East. What is the shortest distance back to his starting point?", "Option B is correct. sqrt(12^2 + 5^2) = sqrt(144 + 25) = sqrt(169) = 13 km.", "Easy", "MCQ", "", {"A": "17 km", "B": "13 km", "C": "15 km", "D": "14 km"}, "B", "What is the Pythagorean triple?"),
    ("A man walks 10 km South, turns left and walks 20 km, turns left again and walks 10 km. How far is he from starting point?", "20 km East. South 10, then East 20, then North 10 cancels South 10. Distance = 20 km.", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What direction is he facing?")
